READ: frac>.02 is the share of pixels a naive GRVI vegetation test calls green, over the
SAME ground in every year. Values near 1.0 mean a global colour cast, not vegetation - the
index is not discriminating there. Wide variation across years means GRVI is not
comparable between them without per-year normalisation.
